course: dictionary
lesson: 383
title: One word, three meanings: Anzac
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Anzac can name a soldier, a special day, or a biscuit. The context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words next to it and ask: is this a person, a day, or something to eat?
explain: «Anzac Day, on 25 April, remembers Australians and New Zealanders who served and died in wars.» Here Anzac Day is a day, because the sentence says when it is and what people remember. «Mum baked Anzac biscuits» is different: the word Anzac tells you what kind of biscuits they are.
explain: Notice the capital letter. Anzac is written with a capital A, because it is a name made from letters. Anzac Day and the Anzacs both use capitals. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Anzac can be a noun (an Anzac, Anzacs) or an adjective (Anzac Day, Anzac biscuits).
fact: An Anzac was a soldier of the Australian and New Zealand Army Corps in the First World War.
fact: The name Anzac is made from the first letters of that army: A-N-Z-A-C.
fact: Anzac Day, 25 April, is a day when Australia and New Zealand remember people who served and died in wars.
fact: Anzac biscuits are sweet biscuits made with oats and golden syrup, from Australia and New Zealand.
exercise: «Anzac Day, on 25 April, remembers Australians and New Zealanders who served and died in wars.» What is Anzac Day? | A soldier's rifle | A kind of petrol station | *A day when Australia and New Zealand remember people who served and died in wars | A sweet biscuit from Australia
exercise: «Mum baked Anzac biscuits with oats and golden syrup.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Anzac? | A word for a loud noise | The name of a month | *A word that describes the biscuits | A name for a soldier
exercise: «Dawn services recall the landing at Gallipoli at dawn in 1915.» Who were the Anzacs? | People who ran the dawn services | *Soldiers of the Australian and New Zealand Army Corps in the First World War | Children who went to school at Gallipoli | Sweet biscuit makers from Turkey
test: «On Anzac Day in Wellington a boy hears the call for a minute's silence.» What does a minute's silence ask people to do? | Sing a loud song | Run to the sea | Open their presents | *Stand still and quiet to remember
test: In which month is Anzac Day? | *April | June | March | December
exam: Ella says every Anzac is a biscuit. Why is she wrong? | *Anzac can also mean a soldier or a day of remembering | Anzac is only a kind of petrol station | Biscuits are never called Anzac | Anzac is a country in Europe
